{
  "key": "sandhya",
  "name": "Sandhya",
  "name_bn": "\u09b8\u09a8\u09cd\u09a7\u09cd\u09af\u09be",
  "premise": "Rooted and literary. The mark is built from the Bangla letterform \u0985 rather than the Latin 'a', so the identity is native to Bangla and the Latin wordmark is the companion \u2014 the reverse of how almost every bilingual brand is put together, and the arrangement your two audiences actually argue for. Colour is a warm ink, close to printing black on uncoated paper, with a single saturated vermilion signal. Vermilion because it is the colour of Bengali print culture and hand-set type, not because it is 'ethnic'; nothing here is folkloric. The register is a small press rather than a software company.",
  "generated_by": "05_colour/engine.py",
